\subsubsection parameters ROS parameters

Reads and maintains the following parameters on the ROS server

- \b "~print_debug" : \b [bool] Enable debug message printing min: False, default: False, max: True
- \b "~print_timestamp" : \b [bool] Enable message timestamp printing min: False, default: False, max: True
- \b "~low_range_limit_m" : \b [double] Low range limit for point cloud debug messages (m) min: 0.0, default: 0.2, max: 25.0
- \b "~high_range_limit_m" : \b [double] High range limit for point cloud debug messages (m) min: 0.0, default: 3.0, max: 25.0
- \b "~low_speed_limit_mps" : \b [double] Low speed limit for point cloud debug messages (m/s) min: -10.0, default: -5.0, max: 10.0
- \b "~high_speed_limit_mps" : \b [double] High speed limit for point cloud debug messages (m/s) min: -10.0, default: 5.0, max: 10.0
- \b "~low_azimuth_limit_deg" : \b [double] Low azimuth limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: -90.0, default: -60.0, max: 90.0
- \b "~high_azimuth_limit_deg" : \b [double] High azimuth limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: -90.0, default: 60.0, max: 90.0
- \b "~low_elevation_limit_deg" : \b [double] Low elevation limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: -90.0, default: -60.0, max: 90.0
- \b "~high_elevation_limit_deg" : \b [double] High elevation limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: -90.0, default: 60.0, max: 90.0
- \b "~low_power_limit" : \b [double] Low power limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: 0.0, default: 0.0, max: 65535.0
- \b "~high_power_limit" : \b [double] High elevation limit for point cloud debug messages (deb) min: 0.0, default: 65535.0, max: 65535.0

